NAME
       readlink - print where a symbolic link points, or a full path

SYNOPSIS
       readlink [-f | -e | -m] [-n] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Without options, readlink prints the target stored in a symbolic link
       (exactly as written when the link was made). It prints nothing and
       fails when FILE is not a symbolic link.

OPTIONS
       -f, --canonicalize
              Follow every link on the way and print the full, absolute path
              of the final file. All parts but the last must exist.

       -e, --canonicalize-existing
              The same, but every part must exist.

       -m, --canonicalize-missing
              The same, with no part required to exist.

       -n, --no-newline
              Do not print a newline at the end.

EXAMPLES
           readlink /etc/localtime
           readlink -f /usr/bin/vi

SEE ALSO
       realpath(1), ln(1), ls(1), namei(1)
